course: dictionary
lesson: 8222
title: Revenge and getting even
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Revenge means hurting or punishing someone because they hurt you or someone you care about. «Years later Esau ran to meet Jacob and hugged him instead of taking revenge.» Esau could have hurt Jacob back, but he chose kindness.
explain: In games and sports, revenge has a lighter meaning: beating a team or player who beat you before. A team that lost last week might say they want revenge in the next match, and they mean they want to win this time.
explain: Stories often show that revenge makes things worse, not better. In real life, you can talk to an adult or solve the problem instead. A punishment is different from revenge: «A punishment like losing screen time is a consequence of what you did, not revenge from your parents.»
fact: Revenge is a noun with no plural: you say revenge, not revenges.
fact: Revenge can also be a verb: to take revenge, or to get revenge.
fact: «Out of revenge» means doing something because you want to hurt someone back.
fact: «Sweet revenge» means the good feeling of beating someone who beat you before.
fact: «Above all, forgiveness is stronger than revenge.» Forgiveness means letting go of anger, so you do not hurt back.
exercise: «Years later Esau ran to meet Jacob and hugged him instead of taking revenge.» What did Esau do instead of taking revenge? | Hit Jacob back | *Hugged Jacob | Ran away and hid | Shouted at the family
exercise: The team that lost last week wants revenge in the next match. What does revenge mean in a game? | Giving the winners a prize | Hurting the other team's players on purpose | Cancelling the match | *Beating the team that beat them before
exercise: «A punishment like losing screen time is a consequence of what you did, not revenge from your parents.» What is a consequence? | A game you play with friends | *Something that happens because of what you did | Something you do to hurt someone back | A gift for being good
test: «Above all, forgiveness is stronger than revenge.» According to this sentence, which is stronger? | Both are exactly the same | Revenge | *Forgiveness | Neither of them
test: Someone hurts you at school. Which is a better choice than revenge? | Tell everyone their secret | *Talk to an adult or help solve the problem | Ignore everyone for ever | Hurt them back a little
exam: Which is the correct noun form of revenge, with no plural? | Revengers | *Revenge | Revenges | Revenged
